d":"986a3378-4828-4f37-8851-18f9e710b94b","position":{"commit_sha":"1df37ab2f7a353ee53f027c0d390b73c8507c0e9","position":"1785614674222898001-986a3378-4828-4f37-8851-18f9e710b94b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan remediation evidence: local Git 2.55 probe produced 'packet: fetch> filter blob:none' for plain fetch inheritance and 'packet: clone> filter blob:none' for clone. The revised oracle matches packet direction/content without hard-coding the actor label. git daemon -h on Git 2.55 has no --git-config option, so the fixture now uses a temporary GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL plus GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 inherited by daemon/upload-pack; it explicitly forbids repository-local allowFilter. Size-guard tests now have non-overlapping names and execute the real workflow blocks against exact-threshold full/blobless repositories.","timestamp":1785612516389964001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Oracle correction during RED: Git 2.55 rejects the planned fixture command 'git repack -a -d --prune=now' because repack has no --prune option. The real-Git fixture uses the equivalent valid deterministic sequence 'git repack -a -d' then 'git prune --expire=now'. No production behavior or acceptance threshold changed.","timestamp":1785614674222898001}],"created_at":1785372539675800001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ac596b6e-ca5f-4cc3-8916-8f26faab9202","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"040e-3f0c-ae86-4212"},{"link_uuid":"75337ce5-2ceb-432b-918d-480031803497","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"3036-cb14-86b5-44a3"}],"description":"Cut CI tickets-store transfer cost across both checkout mechanisms. Measured evidence in session_log 1cb6-d553-6565-49b4 and epic comments: recurring actions/checkout full checkout 1.04 GiB / 59 s versus blob:none 68.7 MiB / 14.3 s; Gerrit verify-identity full tickets fetch 6.73 minutes, with local full 1.4 GB / 66.2 s versus blob:none 22 MB / 3.6 s and 83 MB / 8.6 s after worktree materialization. These recorded baselines do not replace runtime guards.\n\n## Scope and mechanisms\nAdd the published actions/checkout v7 filter input while retaining fetch-depth: 0 and existing credential/ref settings in .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml, .github/workflows/verify-identity.yml, and .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml. These all-history checkouts currently fetch tickets before the mount step.\n\nA later plain git fetch origin +tickets must inherit the named remote filter. Config presence is insufficient because Git records partialclonefilter even when a server ignores it. Prove actual protocol negotiation and missing-object behavior.\n\nIn .github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml both tickets fetches use a direct URL, so named-remote inheritance does not apply. Add --filter=blob:none explicitly to the depth-1 require-ticket fetch and the full-history verify-identity fetch, preserving their different depth semantics. blob:none retains the complete commit graph needed by merge-base and era scoping; depth remains forbidden on the identity fetch.\n\n## Real-Git fixture and protocol oracle\nStart git daemon on localhost with --export-all and --enable=upload-pack. Point GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL at a temporary global config containing uploadpack.allowFilter=true and set GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 in the daemon environment, so daemon/upload-pack inherit filter support. Repository-local uploadpack.allowFilter is forbidden because git daemon ignores it for security. Do not use a file URL. Reserve a loopback port, then retry a socket connection every 100 ms for at most 30 seconds; startup failure raises immediately. The module-scoped pytest fixture uses yield/finally and always terminate()+wait(timeout=5), then kill()+wait() if necessary, so failures cannot leak the daemon.\n\nSet GIT_TRACE_PACKET=<unique tmp trace file> in each git subprocess environment. A Git 2.55 probe observed packet: fetch> filter blob:none for fetch and packet: clone> filter blob:none for clone. Tests must not hard-code the actor label. Require a server capability packet advertising filter plus a client-to-server packet matching packet:\\s+\\S+>\\s+filter blob:none$. Also assert the known tickets blob is reported missing before materialization.\n\nThe fixture commits an incompressible historical blob larger than 140 MiB, removes it, and leaves a tip whose total files are below 1 MiB. After server-side gc:\n- standalone pre-materialization contrast: unfiltered all-history size-pack exceeds REBAR_CHECKOUT_PACK_LIMIT_KIB=102400; blobless size-pack is below 102400;\n- Gerrit post-materialization contrast: unfiltered all-history size-pack exceeds REBAR_TICKETS_PACK_LIMIT_KIB=131072; blobless plus small-tip materialization stays below 131072.\nExecute the actual workflow guard blocks against these repos so broken parsing, units, or comparisons fail.\n\nCapture separate packet traces for plain named-origin inheritance, direct URL with --depth=1 --filter=blob:none, and direct URL full-history with --filter=blob:none. Each must satisfy the capability/request regex and missing-blob oracle.\n\nNever use filter: tree:0: measured 3.57 GiB across 2,255 promisor packs. git worktree add uses unpack-trees -u/check_updates and batch-prefetches missing promisor blobs, unlike the read-tree plus checkout-index footgun in tests/unit/test_snapshot_blobless_747f.py. A real-Git E2E materializes tickets, creates independent local and remote changes, fetches/merges with the B3 ours driver, retains all expected events, and pushes successfully.\n\n## Production guardrails\n- Standalone verify-identity declares REBAR_CHECKOUT_PACK_LIMIT_KIB=102400. Immediately after actions/checkout, parse size-pack from git count-objects -v and fail above that limit.\n- Gerrit verify-identity declares REBAR_TICKETS_PACK_LIMIT_KIB=131072. After filtered fetch and worktree materialization, fail above that limit; this patchset run proves GitHub honored the direct filter.\n- In both identity jobs, snapshot exact git count-objects -v after materialization, run rebar verify-identity, snapshot again, and fail if any line differs. Materialization may fetch tip blobs; identity scanning must add no objects.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each target actions/checkout@v7 step sets filter: blob:none. Tier: parsed workflow. Proving command: pytest tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone_workflows.py -k checkout_filter -v.\n- [ ] Each target checkout retains fetch-depth: 0 and prior credential/ref inputs. Tier: parsed workflow. Proving command: pytest tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone_workflows.py -k checkout_preserves_inputs -v.\n- [ ] Gerrit require-ticket passes --filter=blob:none and retains --depth=1. Tier: parsed workflow. Proving command: pytest tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone_workflows.py -k require_ticket_fetch -v.\n- [ ] Gerrit verify-identity passes --filter=blob:none and has no depth option. Tier: parsed workflow. Proving command: pytest tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone_workflows.py -k identity_fetch -v.\n- [ ] Production guards parse size-pack and use the declared 102400 KiB and 131072 KiB limits. Tier: executable workflow. Proving command: pytest tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone_workflows.py -k pack_guard_contract -v.\n- [ ] The actual standalone guard rejects unfiltered all-history size-pack above 102400 KiB. Tier: real-Git contrast. Proving command: pytest tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py -k standalone_guard_rejects_full -v.\n- [ ] The actual standalone guard accepts blobless pre-materialization size-pack below 102400 KiB. Tier: real-Git contrast. Proving command: pytest tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py -k standalone_guard_accepts_blobless -v.\n- [ ] The actual Gerrit guard rejects unfiltered all-history size-pack above 131072 KiB. Tier: real-Git contrast. Proving command: pytest tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py -k gerrit_guard_rejects_full -v.\n- [ ] The actual Gerrit guard accepts blobless materialized-tip size-pack below 131072 KiB. Tier: real-Git boundary. Proving command: pytest tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py -k gerrit_guard_accepts_materialized -v.\n- [ ] Plain named-origin fetch advertises filter capability, sends filter blob:none, and leaves the known blob missing. Tier: real Git protocol. Proving command: pytest tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py -k named_origin_filter -v.\n- [ ] Depth-1 direct URL fetch advertises filter capability, sends filter blob:none, and leaves the known blob missing. Tier: real Git protocol. Proving command: pytest tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py -k direct_depth_filter -v.\n- [ ] Full-history direct URL fetch advertises filter capability, sends filter blob:none, and leaves the known blob missing. Tier: real Git protocol. Proving command: pytest tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py -k direct_full_filter -v.\n- [ ] Blobless tickets reconverge independent local/remote changes with the ours driver, retain expected events, and push the merge. Tier: real-Git E2E. Proving command: pytest tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py -k reconverges -v.\n- [ ] Standalone identity leaves exact git count-objects -v unchanged. Tier: workflow plus real Git. Proving commands: pytest tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone_workflows.py -k standalone_no_promisor -v and pytest tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py -k standalone_identity_no_promisor -v.\n- [ ] Gerrit identity leaves exact git count-objects -v unchanged. Tier: workflow plus real Git. Proving commands: pytest tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone_workflows.py -k gerrit_no_promisor -v and pytest tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py -k gerrit_identity_no_promisor -v.\n\n## Files and rollback\nFiles: .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml; .github/workflows/verify-identity.yml; .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml; .github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml; tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone_workflows.py; tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py.\n\nRollback is one Gerrit revert restoring prior full fetches and removing paired guards. Do not disable only a failing guard: a threshold trip means the cost regression is real until the filter/server path is repaired or the whole optimization is reverted.\n\nScope: M. Depends on closed B3 040e-3f0c-ae86-4212 and closed B6 3036-cb14-86b5-44a3.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml","reason":"blobless checkout input"},{"path":".github/workflows/verify-identity.yml","reason":"blobless checkout plus pack-size and no-promisor measurements"},{"path":".github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml","reason":"blobless checkout input"},{"path":".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml","reason":"explicit filtered tickets fetches plus pack-size and no-promisor measurements"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone_workflows.py","reason":"parsed workflow contract oracle"},{"path":"tests/integration/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone.py","reason":"real-Git inheritance, direct-fetch, materialization, reconvergence, and no-promisor oracle"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","040e-3f0c-ae86-4212"],["depends_on","3036-cb14-86b5-44a3"],["depends_on","42eb-5789-c798-4dfc"],["parent","42eb-5789-c798-4dfc"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"42eb-5789-c798-4dfc","parent_status_uuid":"1f235554-845a-4dde-bd6e-f50a969d244f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"037b-879e-fe13-47d2","ticket_type":"story","title":"B1: apply filter: blob:none to every CI tickets-branch fetch path","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a9c61278-a3d5-4b7f-9601-c271e9303c23","3526ab7d-f89b-476c-b54d-e682b043e289","d54cabfc-8c69-46f7-b238-74c2af8c592a","ac596b6e-ca5f-4cc3-8916-8f26faab9202","a2363eac-a678-4607-bde3-94a95a552e48","75337ce5-2ceb-432b-918d-480031803497","3ffd5811-2263-4b00-97cb-42e337488888","97afcbf8-e946-4297-83ff-dc187feb109a","6bc205a4-9e7f-4282-b2d7-eb0d474f748b","49bf9b8a-c2ac-41cb-a081-f2e9e559fa48","0ff1feac-5a8e-4674-b8f5-b6240dd31ef2","cfe49df2-6d2c-4b46-9807-dae581fde06e","46b675ac-35e0-4b49-9a3c-5ec686d24bcd","a42395aa-3159-4511-8615-927f7545b107","501e8066-4da6-4e2a-a2a8-59e3091ca630","1f235554-845a-4dde-bd6e-f50a969d244f","26d6fdeb-cdf2-4e96-a46e-a5429c53437d","986a3378-4828-4f37-8851-18f9e710b94b"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785614674222898002,"uuid":"334feb0c-d5c1-4460-909d-f82b535833f2"}